{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdY8JMKRKfdGiEfxTLzJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Jellyfish, a company that makes tools for software developers, sees a different competitive picture in its data than the one that circulates on social media. Nikolas Albarran, its AI product lead, told TechCrunch that if you look at X you would think the race between coding tools is heated, with everyone in the Valley saying Codex is better. In the usage data, he said, it took a long time for Codex to show up at all, and it has begun to since OpenAI released its Astra model.\n\nThe same data shows Claude Code and other tools built on Anthropic models responsible for nearly a third of all proposed code changes submitted for review, in a Jellyfish report covering agentic coding tool use by 276,000 of its customers. That is one analytics vendor's customer base and not the whole market, but it fits the article's observation that Astra looked like a threat to Anthropic and has so far not slowed Anthropic's adoption numbers. Financials Anthropic shared with investors this week point the same way: an operating profit in the second quarter and 900% net revenue retention, meaning the same customers spent nine times as much in Q3 2026 as in Q3 2025.\n\nAlbarran's explanation for the gap is that Anthropic arrived early with strong enterprise sales support, and many teams invested effort in standardizing their workflows around its tools. There is no big enough reason to switch, he said. He also points to small differences in how each tool handles things like agent.md files, which means the cost of changing tools is not zero even if the products are mostly alike.\n\nIf he is right, a better model alone may not be enough for a competitor to move an enterprise customer, because the customer's own configuration work is part of what holds it in place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":2938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1339},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b381f5a8-dc9e-4d73-8484-6effdfbfc570","uuid":"fdd33306-bf30-477a-ba6d-970a1fb4d057","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:19:34.823Z","request_id":"req_011CgdY8J9Qh9jMtKthTBKAD"}
